{"text": " Welcome to Welcome to AI for Agriculture and Agritech. I am so glad you are here. An Agritech startup in Nakuru built an AI tool that tells small-holder maize farmers the optimal data cell based on market price forecasts and their storage condition data. Farmers using the tool earned on average 23% more per kilogram than those selling without it. The tool was built by a data analyst who knew no agriculture before starting but who understood how to ask the right AI questions of agricultural data. By the end of this course you will build a crop yield prediction system using Kenyan weather and soil data and explain its outputs to a farmer or cooperative manager. You will forecast commodity prices for maize, beans and coffee using historical Amis Kenya data and AI modeling. You will analyse post-harvest loss data to identify the highest impact interventions for a real cooperative. You will design and prototype a WhatsApp-based farmer advisory system that delivers personalized recommendations without internet access. And you will deliver a complete AI-powered smart farm proposal for Indege and Bili cooperative that an Agritech investor or NGO could fund. This course has 10 lessons and five hours of content with three hands-on sandboxes. Your final project is AI-powered smart farm proposal for Indege and Bili cooperative, 120 farmers in Meru County. You do not need to code. You do not need a technology background. All you need is the willingness to learn and I will guide you every step of the way. Your first task is waiting below. I will see you in lesson one. Your skills bare fruit.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 7.66, "text": " Welcome to Welcome to AI for Agriculture and Agritech. I am so glad you are here.", "tokens": [50364, 4027, 281, 4027, 281, 7318, 337, 35966, 293, 24454, 642, 339, 13, 286, 669, 370, 5404, 291, 366, 510, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20661797599186973, "compression_ratio": 1.485380116959064